{
  "name": "tick",
  "_about": "The castor bean tick (Ixodes ricinus), a female 3.5 mm long: eight legs and no waist -- a flat teardrop body, red-brown, with a dark hard scutum over its front half; the mouthparts (capitulum) sticking forward like a head -- a basis, two club palps and the barbed hypostome between them; dark brown legs, the front pair held up to sense. Variant: fed, engorged into a grey bean 1 cm long, the legs tiny at its front. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/bugs.py on insectlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
